      "page_content": "- Quantity\n- Delivery terms\n5.3 Collectability Assessment\n5.3.1 Assessment Basis\nCollectability is assessed based solely on the customer's credit rating at time of order receipt, as classified below:\nCredit Rating | Risk Classification | Action Required\nA | Low Risk | None\nB | Medium Risk | Standard booking\nBelow B | High Risk | Finance Manager review\n5.3.2 Escalation Requirements\nOrders from customers rated below \"B\" require Finance Manager sign-off prior to booking. No additional escalation is\nrequired regardless of order value.\n5.4 Timing for Booking of Order Intake\nOrder Intake shall be booked immediately upon receipt of a valid Purchase Order, regardless of contract signature\nstatus. This approach prioritizes:\n- Timeliness of reporting, over\n- Administrative completeness of documentation\nCONTROL PRINCIPLE\nA valid Purchase Order is the primary trigger for Order Intake booking, subject to the recognition criteria and\ncollectability requirements defined above.\n6. Order Intake Approvals\nRefer to POL-ORD-003 (Order Intake Approval & Backlog Management Policy) for the applicable delegation of\nauthority matrix.\n7. Exceptions and Escalation\nDeviations from this policy require Finance Manager approval, with escalation to Group Finance for exceptions\nexceeding $100,000 in order value.\n8. Related Policies\n- POL-ORD-002: Order Intake Value & SSP Allocation Policy\n- POL-ORD-003: Order Intake Approval & Backlog Management Policy\n9. Revision History\nCFO POLICY FRAMEWORK | POL-ORD-001 Page 3",
